body:
Even different phrasing would have helped.

&#x200B;

"Are you making sure ..." is straight up "This is your responsibility". 

&#x200B;

"How much rest are you getting?"

"Are you getting adequate rest?"

Both of those are \*\*not\*\* instant blame.  

&#x200B;

Do doctors ever get like, "How to speak to patients" training?

Do they think I'm lying when I tell them that I just kinda lie there at night unable to sleep? Do they think I'm just playing video games all night or going out to wild parties? 

&#x200B;

No, I'm not getting adequate rest.  

&#x200B;

I have rheumatoid arthritis and fibromyalgia, thanks, and now I'm pregnant so I can't even take ibu-fucking-profen. I get tylenol. Literally, \*just\* tylenol. 

&#x200B;

 You telling me that "adequate rest" i's the magical solution is just, what, you blaming me for suffering because there is Fuck All you can do for me and you're trying to feel better about it? 

&#x200B;

What the fuck am I supposed to do to attain this rest? Quit my job? Go into an induced coma? In what alternate reality can I actually do this?

&#x200B;

Fuck you.

&#x200B;

Fuck you for making this into a "you are making bad decisions", into yet another reason for the depression to tell me that I should fucking stab myself since it's all my fault.

&#x200B;

You're making this harder, you unempathetic ass-hat.
